+### claim: account-surface-finds-planted
+- claim: A deterministic, offline, read-only audit of a consumer repository's account-flow code finds the planted defect of every class it reports as violated, without flagging a safe twin or a decoy.
+- kind: quant
+- evidence: PRE-REGISTERED 2026-10-13 (road-to-account-surface-detector Phase 1.2), BEFORE any `check_account_surface` code exists -- the registering commit carries the frozen corpus and this entry and no detector, which is what makes this a pre-registration rather than a description of what a detector turned out to catch. BASELINE: zero, by construction. Nothing in the tree reads a consumer's login code: the scanners under `src/scripts/` check the package itself, the consumer's agent configuration, tool output or secrets; `grade_target_readiness.ts` grades thirteen dimensions, none of them authentication; and the prelaunch AUTH area is filled by the model with `unknown` as its honest default (`src/skills/launch-readiness/SKILL.md`). CORPUS: the frozen set at `tests/fixtures/account-surface/`, two stacks (a PHP framework shape, a Node/TypeScript shape), with twelve planted defects across eight lexical classes, a safe twin per planted file at the SAME basename so a path predicate cannot separate them, and six decoys that name every keyed word -- a digest over a file, a bucketing salt, a pagination token, a pepper read from the environment, a login surface that changes presentation only, and prose about passwords. Ground truth at `tests/fixtures/account-surface/ground-truth.json`, frozen before the detector. METRICS, PER CLASS: recall over that class's planted defects, and false positives over the twins and decoys. BARS, fixed here and not after the run: recall at or above 0.90 and false positives at or below 0.03 per class. WHAT THOSE BARS MEAN AT THIS CORPUS SIZE, stated because a proportion implies a precision the corpus does not have: a class carries one or two planted files, so its recall can only be 0, 0.5 or 1.0 and the 0.90 bar is in practice "every planted defect of this class"; the negative set is eighteen files in total, so the 0.03 bar is in practice "no false positive anywhere". A larger corpus would make the bars continuous; this one does not, and reporting 0.90 as if it tolerated a miss would overstate the measurement. HARD GATE, and it is the reason a class can fail while scoring perfect recall: a flagged decoy is a classification FAILURE that fails that class REGARDLESS of recall. A detector that finds everything by flagging everything is the failure a recall threshold cannot see. FALSIFICATION: (1) a decoy or a safe twin is flagged; (2) a class misses its recall bar; (3) the corpus cannot be scored against its ground truth, in which case the claim is UNDERPOWERED rather than dropped -- an unscoreable corpus says nothing about a detector. ON A CLASS MISSING ITS BAR: that class stays `suspected`-only in the detector's own output rather than the detector shipping a `violated` it did not earn. SCOPE, and it is a restriction this entry imposes on itself: twelve planted files over two stacks is one measurement of LEXICAL classes on a frozen corpus. It establishes whether THESE patterns separate THESE files, and generalises to neither a third stack nor a real consumer repository nor any defect the corpus does not carry. ABSENCE IS NEVER A RESULT: a class finding no pattern is reported as undecided, never as a passing account surface, so no figure here may be read as evidence that a login flow is safe.
